Track 1: Sea Smoke Chews the Pier
- Story & Context: When the 50,000-ton bulk carrier Caroni Star lost its rudder during a sudden cold-water fog inversion off Point Lisas, Carlyle Baptiste stood on the seawall with his contact-mic’d flute, blasting frantic high-register trills into the whiteout to guide the harbor tugs away from the pylons. The ship's twin diesel horn roared back in deafening four-second intervals, inadvertently locking into a ferocious 2:3 counterpoint with Baptiste's breathless melodies while Devon hammered the salt-encrusted mooring bollards with iron rebar. As the freighter's bow missed the concrete gantry by a mere twenty feet, Carlyle screamed into his megaphone over the wash of diesel exhaust and boiling foam, "Blow your horn, big iron beast, we dancing on the mud tonight!"
