Track 2: "Is That a Halo or a Flare, Cap?"
- Story & Context: Drunk on overproof rum inside the humid, vibrating wheelhouse of an idle cargo tender, radar tech Myron De Freitas confessed to intentionally scrambling the harbor acoustic logs after optical halos around the navigation buoys made him hallucinate carnival dancers on the water. His trembling fingers accidentally left the bridge radio channel open while Baptiste’s flute pierced through the speaker horn in ragged, multiphonic bursts, imitating the distressed air-pipes of an incoming bauxite freighter blind in the soup. As the ship’s hull groaned against the rubber fenders with a sickening screech, Myron’s voice leaked across every receiver in the bay: "You see a halo in the cloud, but I just see my pension sinking."
